@startuml agent-registration
!theme plain
title Legacy readable-token view: First consumer: caller-composed plan, account, broker binding, curator-run under the agent UID

participant "Orchestrator" as O
participant "swarma-dispatcher\n(service account swarma-dispatcher)" as D
participant "swarma-user-manager\n(root, closed op schema)" as H
participant "Broker" as B
participant "swarma-user-launcher\n(root, closed launch schema)" as L
participant "curator-run\n(agent OS account, narrow one-shot mode)" as E

O -> O: compose and resolve profiles; protected credential metadata only\n(no token in plan); record resolved launch PATH in plan digest
O -> D: start a worker: immutable plan, accounts, until end of task
D -> D: check O may start it; retain root request_id; derive distinct create/bind/launch effect IDs
D -> B: revocation.check: exact caller/lease chains; context prepare
B --> D: not_revoked | revoked | unavailable, with check-point revocation sequence
break revoked or unavailable
  D --> O: refuse before account creation; no downstream effect
end
D -> H: sudo swarma-user-manager (no arguments)\nstdin: user.create {kind: agent, label: dev-7f3}, create effect ID
H -> H: under the helper lock: allocate UID, fresh random 128-bit generation; ledger (creating → active)
H --> D: {username: worker-dev-7f3, uid: 30412, generation: 4a91c5e03b2d4788a649d70fc62e15bd}
D -> D: sign leaf grant: subject agent:4a91c5e03b2d4788a649d70fc62e15bd, depth 0,\nnarrowed from its own grant (chain to the root)
D -> D: binding request must carry recorded admission class for UID/generation;\nencoding unpublished; not inferred from username
D -> B: bind {uid 30412, generation 4a91c5e03b2d4788a649d70fc62e15bd, label, profiles [dev],\nchain [leaf, dispatcher grant, root],\ncaller {chain [caller grant, …, root], intersection}, request_id: bind effect ID, expires_at}
B -> B: peer is a dispatcher principal; verify admission-class evidence;\nrefuse untrusted/unavailable class or R-ALLSTOP freeze;\nroot-owned ledger.json (helper §4.5):\n4a91c5e03b2d4788a649d70fc62e15bd active, kind agent, created by this dispatcher;\nverify both chains, every edge incl. the leaf;\nleaf within the caller intersection; current revocations and R-TIME max/min checks; untrusted time or restore fence? refuse
break untrusted/unavailable class evidence or R-ALLSTOP freeze
  B --> D: refuse bind; codes unpublished (§18.16-§18.17)
  D --> O: no binding or launch
end
B -> B: pre-admission refusal: no intent; fresh retry checks (R-OUTCOME);\nserialize receiver journal; persist admitted bind intent before mutation;\nrepeat class/freeze gates before authority creation;\npersist result/current target state before acknowledgement
B --> D: binding/1 {binding_id}
opt bind acknowledgement lost
  D -> B: effect.observe: original bind request_id, bind, canonical-argument digest
  B --> D: recorded (result + current target state) | pending | rolled_back |\nnot_recorded | unavailable | contradictory
  break binding not conclusively present and active
    D -> D: hold/reconcile allocation; no launch or automatic replacement create
  end
end
D -> D: close the broker connection
D -> B: revocation.check: exact chains; context start
B --> D: not_revoked | revoked | unavailable, with check-point revocation sequence
break revoked or unavailable
  D --> O: refuse before privileged start; reconcile existing effects
end
D -> D: owning claim and cancellation gate still required
D -> L: sudo swarma-user-launcher (no arguments)\nstdin: launch.start {generation: 4a91c5e03b2d4788a649d70fc62e15bd, execution_id, epoch,\nexecutor: curator-run, plan: base64, request_id: launch effect ID}
L -> L: ledger: 4a91c5e03b2d4788a649d70fc62e15bd active; executor digest approved;\napply user-manager helper §7 descriptor lifecycle (R-FD3);\nprotected immutable plan on FD3; root receipt and UID/GID transition
L -> E: exec approved curator-run as uid 30412 (plan on FD3)
E -> E: verify and execute caller-composed plan;\nno composition or profile resolution; no network except broker
E -> B: fresh connection (trusted-class lease flow: lease-at-launch)
D --> O: execution handle (run_id, execution_id, generation, binding_id)
note over D,L
  Privileged payloads are abbreviated, not copyable schemas.
  Helper §7 owns execution_id/epoch/FD3/start-receipt and descriptor lifecycle.
  Only dispatcher invokes privileged starts; host uses host_start (R-START).
  Dispatcher is a socket service from slice 0; no dispatcher sudo entry.
  Point-in-time verdict never waives final bind/lease/renew checks.
end note
note over O,B
  If O was provisioned by C, C signs O's narrowed caller delegation
  after generation-bound key registration; D only verifies/records (R-DELEG).
  W's caller chain retains C, separately from D's lease chain (§16.1).
  Registration alone grants no spawn authority; recursive provisioning
  remains refused until bootstrap publication and qualification.
end note
note over O: D-PATH: protected launch tools → admitted base PATH → protected manager dispatcher.\nNo repository .agents/bin executes in a managed launch.
note over E: Narrow executor intake is an approved versioned target (D-EXECUTOR);\nLauncher SPEC §10 / Decision 0021 amendment publish its command/plan contract. Board runner and host call dispatcher.
note over D,B
  E-rebind uses binding replacement for this same UID/generation;
  no account recreation, no widening, fresh prepare verdict and final checks.
  Old-binding tombstone survives; old leases end; replay never reactivates.
  Exact replacement intake unpublished (§18.11); see binding-replacement.puml.
  No helper broker principal. All platform-service calls release state locks
  with per-record in-flight ownership and late-result fencing (R-LOCK, §13.1).
  R-SESSION permit is session-scoped; every physical start keeps its own claim.
end note
note over O,B
  R-UNTRUSTED: slice 0/user-manager v0 refuse untrusted class.
  Later workplaces have zero egress, no broker binding/lease and no local loop.
  Circle membership never changes a remote identity's workplace placement.
  Host loops, including standing loops, require trusted class AND local agent placement (§4.2).
  Membership alone grants neither host-loop authority nor a review-role grant.
  R-ALLSTOP closes admission; revocation.check unavailable while frozen.
  Prior verdict never bypasses class/freeze checks; mappings unpublished (§18.16-§18.17).
  Workspace materialization/export belong to dispatcher R-TRANSFER;
  worker .git/history are never platform input; broker holds no workspace.
end note
@enduml

@startuml agent-registration-secret-free
!theme plain
title Proposed secret-free view: agent-registration — inactive
participant "Admitted launch / dispatcher" as D
participant "Broker" as B
participant "Spending service\nown kernel identity + generation" as G
participant "Agent-side runner" as R
D -> B : retain original caller narrowing chain / launch binding
G -> B : fresh fixed-role connection; verify broker UID
B -> B : compatible dialect; current service generation/class/placement\nservice authority and account; no hold/freeze/restore fence
break missing dialect, retired identity or unavailable state
  B --> G : refuse; no service material or activation
end
B --> G : own service lease; not caller authority
R -> G : protected launch / profile / caller context
G -> G : qualify listener owner/generation and served policy\nmap random placeholder to lease / generation / launch / account
G --> R : placeholder only on qualified channel
note over D,R
  R-EXEC / FD3 / plan-object / startup and later re-exec checks remain.
  Static UID allowance or circle membership is insufficient.
  Workplaces: zero egress, no lease. Local-only first; donors B/C CLOSED.
  Exact new binding/intake formats and permissions remain unpublished.
end note

legend bottom
  Separate proposed secret-free mode, document revision 1: INACTIVE / UNQUALIFIED.
  Semantic responsibilities only; no new v0 methods, fields, codes or record formats.
  [[../spec/secret-free-mode.md Owning proposed contract and qualification gates]]
endlegend
@enduml
